Below is the exact request you would send to VirusTotal to retrieve the **sub‑domain** objects that are related to `example.org`.  
Only the object IDs and any context attributes are returned – no other fields are requested.

```http
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/related?relationship=subdomains&limit=10&cursor=abc
Host: www.virustotal.com
Accept: application/json
X-Apikey: my_api
```

---

### Expected JSON response (trimmed to IDs & context)

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "sub1.example.org",
      "type": "domain",
      "attributes": {
        "last_analysis_stats": { ... },
        "last_analysis_date": 1700000000,
        "last_analysis_results": { ... }
      },
      "relationships": { ... },
      "context_attributes": {
        "relationship_type": "subdomain",
        "confidence": 0.95
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sub2.example.org",
      "type": "domain",
      "attributes": { ... },
      "relationships": { ... },
      "context_attributes": {
        "relationship_type": "subdomain",
        "confidence": 0.92
      }
    },
    ...
  ],
  "links": {
    "self": "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/related?relationship=subdomains&limit=10&cursor=abc",
    "next": "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/related?relationship=subdomains&limit=10&cursor=xyz"
  },
  "meta": {
    "cursor": "xyz",
    "total": 42
  }
}
```

**What you’ll actually receive**

- `id`: the unique identifier of each related object (e.g., a sub‑domain name).  
- `context_attributes`: any metadata that VirusTotal attaches to the relationship (often includes `relationship_type`, `confidence`, etc.).  
- All other fields (`attributes`, `relationships`, etc.) are omitted from the response because they were not requested.

If you need only the IDs and context attributes, you can parse the `data` array and extract those two keys for each element.
